# {{NAME}}

A Cadencr custom tab: a small web app Cadencr shows as a tab on every
conversation page of the projects you enable it for.

## Develop

```sh
npm install
npm run dev     # rebuilds dist/ on every save; Cadencr reloads the tab
npm run build   # type-check, then a one-off build
```

Open any conversation, add the tab from the **+** menu, and keep `npm run dev`
running while you edit `src/`.

## Files

- `tab.json` — the manifest: id, name, label, permissions. Cadencr validates
  it on every change; problems show in **Settings → Custom tabs**.
- `src/` — the React app. `src/App.tsx` is the place to start.
- `dist/` — the build Cadencr loads (not committed).
- `vendor/` — the Cadencr SDK and UI kit, until they are published to npm.
- `INSTRUCTION.md` — the full contract, written for coding agents.
